A||N||15||DaRkLoRD||Thundersnow..||||6||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||12-12-2000||03:30 AM||||Tonight I got to watch a fairly rare weather event, which meteorologists call "thundersnow". we're having a bit of a snowstorm here in Toronto, and there's a thunderstorm going on as well..... I have never seen that before tonight.. it's weird, and very cool!<P>there's the howling of the wind, the snow hitting my window, flash of lightning, and the occasional crack of thunder.. it's definitely a cool experience. Anyone else from TO see this?<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||6
Z||000001||Raydar||12-12-2000||09:55 AM||||I actually saw this in Atlanta, many years ago. The thunder and lightning were not very intense, but we ended up with about 4-5 inches of snow. Hasn't happened here, since.<BR>It wouldn't surprise me, though. Most of our infrequent snowstorms are caused by moist *tropical* air blowing up from the Gulf of Mexico, which floats over cold air that blows in from New England.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||12-12-2000||09:57 AM||||Well I'm not from Toronto, but just a little south of you in Buffalo, and we have had that type of a storm twice this year already.  Back in Novemeber, when the city got shut down bby the snow, there was a TON of lightning and thunder.  I never saw anything like it.  <BR>The church by my house got struck by lightning and the top of the steeple started on fire and nearly burnt the church down.  It ended up being nearly 200k in damages  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>We also had some thunder and lightning a little over a week ago too. But we didn't get any last night.  All we got was 15 degree weather, a couple inches of snow, and 55mph wind gusts  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  And this is relativley good weather for us this winter, lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000003||FieroLisa||12-12-2000||12:25 PM||||Well late last night I was chatting with a friend who lives in SW PA and he said the sky was orange (at 1 am) and was doing some crazy stuff. When he woke up in the morning it was like a tornado had blown through, pieces of house were missing and trees down and christmas decorations everywhere.<P> <P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>*Updated Website* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||btoth||12-12-2000||01:04 PM||||We had 50mph winds and snow last night!!!  Could barely get to school this morning.  All of the traffic lights were out and there were tree branches everwhere on the road.  And of course, the Fiero's doors were frozen as were the roads... not a fun trip.<P>We did have thunder and snow a few weeks ago... I didn't even know that could happen till i saw it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||12-12-2000||01:19 PM||||Doomsday prophecies aside, this year has seen the weirdest weather I can remember in my whole life..<P>severe weather is increasing.. disease is getting worse (ebola etc, and bacteria which is resistant to antibiotics) and now war is brewing in the mideast.. kinda makes ya wonder though...<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||AkursedX||12-12-2000||04:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>Doomsday prophecies aside, this year has seen the weirdest weather I can remember in my whole life..<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The weather most part is due to global warming.  It might not be any hotter yet, but this is just the start.  The slow raising of the earth's temperature is creating more and more irregular weather patterns.  That's why we have been getting such severe weather (extreme heat, drought, huge snowfalls, bitter cold...etc.)  It's just that it doesn't last as long.  <P>Those doomsday prophecies are starting to make people wonder though...<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||12-12-2000||04:43 PM||||We know *why* they're happening now, what's freaky is that they were predicted, for this exact time period, almost 2,000 years ago.<BR>Including the war in the mideast.. which seems closer to happening now than any time in the recent past.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fformula88||12-12-2000||05:33 PM||||We had a lot of lightning out here by the airport in Buffalo last night.  Tons of rain/snow/hail with 60 MPH wind gusts and tons of lightning.  It was very spectacular!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||12-12-2000||05:49 PM||||For a some interesting reading. There is a book called "The Quickening" the author is "Art Bell". It describes all the events (weather, desease, world governments, Global views, Solar changes, UFO's, etc) and how it will eventually lead to a much different world. You should check it out.||||reg||1
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||12-12-2000||05:52 PM||||I used to listen to Art Bell a lot, but not so much since he suddenly quit for a month or 2 back in 1998.. I just never got back into the show. I've never spoken to him personally, but I used to know his site's webmaster, Keith Rowland.<P>FYI, Art Bell has an all night radio talk show which deals with various scientific, paranormal or otherwise "weird" topics.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 12-12-2000).]||||reg||1
